Subject: [PATCH 4/6] docs: describe stable AVX-512 support

---
 curve25519-dalek/README.md | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/README.md b/curve25519-dalek/README.md
index c918d69..dbf34ca 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/README.md
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/README.md
@@ -148,16 +148,20 @@ $ cargo build --target i686-unknown-linux-gnu
 
 ## SIMD backend
 
-The specific SIMD backend (AVX512 / AVX2 / `serial` default) is selected automatically at runtime, depending on the currently available CPU features, and whether Rust nightly is being used for compilation. The precise conditions are specified below.
+The specific SIMD backend (AVX512 / AVX2 / `serial` default) is selected
+automatically at runtime, depending on the currently available CPU features.
+AVX512 requires Rust 1.89 or newer, where its target features and intrinsics
+are stable, or an older nightly compiler.
 
 For a given CPU feature, you can also specify an appropriate `-C target_feature` to build a binary which assumes the required SIMD instructions are always available. Don't do this if you don't have a good reason.
 
 | Backend | `RUSTFLAGS`                               | Requires nightly? |
 | :---    | :---                                      | :---              |
 | avx2    | `-C target_feature=+avx2`                 | no                |
-| avx512  | `-C target_feature=+avx512ifma,+avx512vl` | yes               |
+| avx512  | `-C target_feature=+avx512ifma,+avx512vl` | before Rust 1.89  |
 
-If compiled on a non-nightly compiler, `curve25519-dalek` will not include AVX512 code, and therefore will never select it at runtime.
+Stable compilers before Rust 1.89 do not include AVX512 code and fall back to
+AVX2 or the serial backend.
 
